WEBVTT

00:02.045 --> 00:03.671
[Narrator] Previously on lost:

00:03.755 --> 00:06.633
You gotta trust me.
I am trying to help you.

00:06.716 --> 00:09.719
Do I know you?
— I'm George minkowski.

00:09.802 --> 00:12.805
Communications officer.
— where is the radio room?

00:12.889 --> 00:15.016
I'll take you there.

00:15.099 --> 00:17.560
How do we get out of here?

00:17.644 --> 00:20.063
Through the door.

00:20.146 --> 00:22.982
Looks like you guys
have a friend on this boat.

00:24.317 --> 00:25.860
You're pregnant?

00:27.403 --> 00:31.157
Juliet. She was their fertility doctor
studying pregnant women.

00:31.241 --> 00:35.370
The reason the others wanted her baby
was for research.

00:35.453 --> 00:39.499
What happens to pregnant women?
— they die.

00:39.582 --> 00:42.752
You want me to help you and your baby.
I have answers.

00:42.835 --> 00:46.589
But you have to come with me now.
— the baby isn't Jin's.

00:48.591 --> 00:52.720
I'm gonna determine the date of
conception. If you got pregnant here...

00:54.347 --> 00:56.307
We'll cross that bridge
when we come to it.

00:56.391 --> 01:00.937
The baby was conceived eight weeks ago.
You got pregnant on the island.

01:01.020 --> 01:03.564
So how long do I have?

01:05.358 --> 01:09.362
Most of the women made it into
the middle of their second trimester.

01:09.445 --> 01:11.406
Nobody made it to their third.

01:27.463 --> 01:29.007
[Man] Lapidus!

01:39.183 --> 01:40.685
You ready?

01:41.728 --> 01:43.062
I'll be up.

01:45.481 --> 01:47.400
Don't be late, frank.

02:00.288 --> 02:03.583
Regina. — frank.

02:03.666 --> 02:08.046
I didn't hear you.
— sorry. Didn't mean to spook ya.

02:08.129 --> 02:10.923
The captain wanted me to bring
these guys some grub.

02:14.385 --> 02:16.429
You know, your book's upside down.

02:24.354 --> 02:25.813
Just trying to help.

02:32.111 --> 02:35.823
Thought I'd check in on you guys,
bring you some food.

02:35.907 --> 02:39.035
How you feeling, by the way?
— much better, thanks.

02:39.118 --> 02:43.122
Why are we held captive? We had nothing
to do with minkowski's death.

02:43.206 --> 02:48.544
Nothing to do with minkowski. Captain
wasn't happy you busted out of sick bay

02:48.628 --> 02:51.005
and into our radio room.
— we didn't bust out.

02:51.089 --> 02:53.508
The door was left open.

02:53.633 --> 02:57.095
And we assumed it was you.
— why the hell would I do that?

02:58.471 --> 03:00.807
Any contact
with our people on the beach?

03:01.641 --> 03:04.560
No luck. Something
must've happened to their phone.

03:08.272 --> 03:10.566
Lima beans?

03:10.650 --> 03:13.111
Sorry, we had a problem
in the kitchen.

03:14.028 --> 03:15.613
Just stay put, all right?

03:17.490 --> 03:19.492
I still want to talk to the captain.

03:21.160 --> 03:22.537
No, you don't.

03:26.249 --> 03:29.001
Regina.
— [door unlatches, opens]

03:38.261 --> 03:40.888
[Speaks Korean]

03:42.932 --> 03:46.144
[Speaks Korean]

04:07.665 --> 04:09.417
Let's talk about baby names.

04:10.918 --> 04:13.129
Good. You're getting better.

04:14.213 --> 04:15.298
But no, Jin.

05:09.143 --> 05:12.104
[Action music on TV]

05:16.609 --> 05:19.362
[Talking in Korean on TV]

05:45.137 --> 05:47.390
[Dialing]

05:47.473 --> 05:49.392
[Woman speaking Korean]

05:49.475 --> 05:52.228
[Groaning]

07:13.309 --> 07:15.311
[Groans]

07:40.127 --> 07:42.254
[Cell phone rings]

08:08.864 --> 08:09.907
What happened?

08:09.990 --> 08:13.869
You mean before or after
the redhead knocked me out?

08:15.371 --> 08:16.580
She hit you?

08:16.664 --> 08:19.875
When I ran into them
on my way back from Locke's camp.

08:19.959 --> 08:21.210
Why would she do that?

08:22.378 --> 08:26.924
Guess she didn't want to explain why she
was on her way to a poison gas factory.

08:29.051 --> 08:31.345
Juliet told Jack it was a power station.

08:31.470 --> 08:34.432
Why would Juliet lie about that?

08:34.515 --> 08:35.725
Force of habit.

08:37.601 --> 08:40.396
Why were they going there?
— to turn it off.

08:40.479 --> 08:43.858
Deactivate the gas. They wanted
to earn some brownie points.

08:46.694 --> 08:49.947
Do you think they're
really going to rescue us?

08:50.030 --> 08:52.908
In the time they've been here,
they've talked about a lot.

08:52.992 --> 08:56.287
And none involved rescuing us.

09:17.016 --> 09:18.017
Good morning.

09:20.436 --> 09:21.771
Good morning.

09:21.854 --> 09:24.899
I hope they resolve
their kitchen issues.

09:31.822 --> 09:32.865
Sayid.

09:35.117 --> 09:36.619
What's that?

09:43.083 --> 09:45.002
It's a note.

09:46.712 --> 09:51.008
Three days ago,
when I was in Locke's camp,

09:51.091 --> 09:53.552
Ben claimed he had a spy on this boat.

10:13.656 --> 10:16.742
Hello. My name is sun.

10:16.826 --> 10:19.745
Hi, sun. Hi. I'm Daniel.

10:23.791 --> 10:25.751
Something I can help you with?

10:26.877 --> 10:28.754
I'm two months pregnant.

10:30.422 --> 10:34.218
Oh, you're... wow. That's...

10:34.301 --> 10:38.180
Congratulations.
— so you're here to rescue us?

10:42.643 --> 10:44.770
It's a simple question.

10:44.895 --> 10:47.982
Are you or are you not
going to rescue us?

10:49.942 --> 10:52.111
The thing is, um...

10:54.405 --> 10:56.574
It's not really my call, sun.

10:57.700 --> 10:59.493
Then whose call is it?

11:03.789 --> 11:05.291
Thank you.

11:07.418 --> 11:09.670
Can you pass the cereal?

11:17.678 --> 11:20.556
Pretty good English, Jin.
— thank you.

11:20.639 --> 11:24.351
I understand better than I speak.

11:26.145 --> 11:28.856
Sun been teaching you
or you just picking it up?

11:28.981 --> 11:32.443
Oh, sun teach me. Sawyer, too.

11:33.611 --> 11:37.656
Sun is better. — I bet.

11:40.618 --> 11:43.537
Hey, sun. How you feeling?

11:43.621 --> 11:45.998
I'm good, thank you.

11:47.499 --> 11:50.586
The morning sickness has stopped,
which has been nice.

11:51.503 --> 11:52.713
That's good.

11:53.547 --> 11:57.760
Well, if you need anything,
just let me know. Ok?

12:03.182 --> 12:05.100
Would you like some breakfast?

12:43.430 --> 12:44.974
What are you doing?

12:47.726 --> 12:51.438
I needed another bottle
of those vitamins you gave me.

12:51.522 --> 12:54.984
The prenatals.
— you could have just asked.

12:55.067 --> 12:57.653
You're right. I should have.

12:57.736 --> 12:59.863
What happened to the
last ones I gave you?

13:01.532 --> 13:04.159
Sorry?
— the last bottle I gave you.

13:07.371 --> 13:08.914
Are you planning a trip?

13:10.290 --> 13:12.376
Please, just give me the vitamins.

13:14.253 --> 13:16.046
Where are you going, sun?

13:18.841 --> 13:21.635
We're going to Locke's camp.
— what?

13:23.220 --> 13:26.807
Why?
— because I don't trust these people.

13:26.890 --> 13:29.018
Whether you trust them or not,
you can't go.

13:29.101 --> 13:33.897
Locke doesn't want to leave the island.
I've told you, pregnant women,

13:33.981 --> 13:35.357
they don't survive here.

13:35.482 --> 13:38.193
Yes, you did tell me that.

13:39.945 --> 13:41.196
You don't believe me?

13:42.948 --> 13:46.660
Look, I know I've
been less than truthful

13:46.785 --> 13:51.123
about certain things since coming here,
but I promise you, sun, I promise you,

13:51.206 --> 13:53.459
I'm not lying about this.

13:55.502 --> 13:59.798
After everything you've confided in me,
I should at least have your trust.

14:02.801 --> 14:06.263
Claire's baby is fine. I feel fine.

14:06.346 --> 14:10.559
All I have are your stories
that I'm going to get sick.

14:10.642 --> 14:13.979
I'm going to do what's best for me
and for my baby.

14:14.063 --> 14:17.816
Because no, I don't trust you.

14:26.325 --> 14:29.453
[Gasping]

14:34.917 --> 14:36.376
[Gasps]

15:55.247 --> 15:56.832
Taxi!

16:11.013 --> 16:12.222
[Honks horn]

16:21.607 --> 16:22.649
[Shouts]

16:34.828 --> 16:36.330
[Shouts]

17:07.319 --> 17:08.862
[Dragon roar sound]

17:21.750 --> 17:23.752
[Dragon roar sound]

17:31.385 --> 17:34.096
Once you hit this stream,
you wanna head northwest.

17:34.221 --> 17:37.099
Pretty much in a straight line
for about a day and a half.

17:37.182 --> 17:40.769
Thank you.
— I'm gonna have to tell Jack.

17:42.479 --> 17:44.398
I'll give you a long head start.

17:44.523 --> 17:46.984
I'd tell him,
but he wouldn't understand.

17:47.067 --> 17:49.027
No, he wouldn't.

17:51.196 --> 17:53.407
You better get going.

17:54.866 --> 17:56.910
Be safe, ok? — thank you.

17:57.035 --> 17:59.371
She's not going anwvhere.

17:59.496 --> 18:03.333
Sun, this is a bad idea.
— what concern is it of yours?

18:03.417 --> 18:07.671
Do you understand your
wife's medical condition right now?

18:08.880 --> 18:11.883
Translate for me. — no.

18:13.719 --> 18:16.596
Your wife is very sick.

18:17.389 --> 18:20.851
If she doesn't get off this island
in three weeks, she will die.

18:23.854 --> 18:25.772
[Speaks Korean]

18:27.274 --> 18:32.321
If you let her go,
your wife is in danger, Jin. Danger.

18:34.031 --> 18:37.117
Where sun go, I go.

18:39.953 --> 18:42.414
Sun. Please.

18:47.961 --> 18:49.421
Jin.

18:50.839 --> 18:52.591
Your wife had an affair.

18:56.845 --> 19:00.515
What?
— sun was with another man.

19:04.269 --> 19:06.480
She thought the baby was his.

19:36.218 --> 19:37.344
[Speaks Korean]

20:21.888 --> 20:23.932
Hey! You going fishing?

20:25.600 --> 20:28.186
Mind if I tag along?

20:31.440 --> 20:35.193
Oh, I'm sorry.
I didn't mean to interrupt.

20:35.277 --> 20:37.237
No. Come.

20:37.320 --> 20:38.864
You sure?

20:40.949 --> 20:43.535
Yes. Come.

21:06.391 --> 21:09.144
We're the only two married guys
on the island.

21:11.730 --> 21:13.315
Married.

21:14.608 --> 21:18.528
Married.
— yeah, well, not to each other, no.

21:18.612 --> 21:20.363
You got it.

21:21.990 --> 21:24.159
It's not easy, is it?

21:24.242 --> 21:27.996
I mean, it's wonderful,
but let's face it.

21:28.079 --> 21:31.374
Every decision that you make
takes twice as long.

21:31.458 --> 21:33.627
You always gotta talk them into it.

21:39.132 --> 21:42.677
Rose... has cancer.

21:45.805 --> 21:49.267
She's sick. Dying.

21:51.269 --> 21:54.105
Well, she was dying.

21:54.231 --> 21:56.191
She says she's better now.

21:57.275 --> 22:01.321
She says it's this place. The island.

22:03.698 --> 22:08.495
But when the camp split up,
I was sure she'd want to go with Locke.

22:09.829 --> 22:14.584
Why would she want to leave the island
and risk getting sick again?

22:16.962 --> 22:20.215
Then why do you stay with Jack?

22:20.298 --> 22:22.425
Because it was the right thing to do.

22:23.802 --> 22:27.472
Locke, he's a murderer.

22:30.934 --> 22:32.811
It's all about Karma, Jin.

22:33.728 --> 22:35.397
You know Karma?

22:37.315 --> 22:39.901
You make bad choices,
bad things happen.

22:39.985 --> 22:42.237
But you make good choices, good...

22:42.320 --> 22:44.656
Hey, hey! You got one!

22:44.781 --> 22:47.492
Here. Pull it in!

22:47.576 --> 22:52.330
Wow! Look at that!
You see? Now, that's Karma.

22:54.874 --> 22:56.918
We must be the good guys.

23:05.135 --> 23:07.846
[Distant clanging]

23:11.683 --> 23:14.519
How long is that gonna go on for?

23:14.603 --> 23:17.105
Can't they fix whatever is causing it?

23:17.188 --> 23:19.399
That sound is not mechanical.

23:19.482 --> 23:22.694
You think somebody's doing that?

23:22.777 --> 23:25.905
Somebody's banging on those pipes?
— exactly what I think.

23:25.989 --> 23:27.157
[Door unlatches]

23:29.534 --> 23:32.454
Gentlemen, thanks for your Patience.

23:33.955 --> 23:36.374
The captain would like to see you now.

23:52.557 --> 23:56.394
Where's the helicopter?
— lapidus is running an errand.

23:56.519 --> 23:58.980
What kind of errand?
— I'm the doctor.

23:59.064 --> 24:01.900
I don't know where he's going.
— to the island?

24:02.692 --> 24:04.986
[Doctor] Know anwvhere else
he could land?

24:05.070 --> 24:06.613
[Sayid] What's he going to do?

24:06.696 --> 24:08.406
[Doctor] I said I'm just the doctor.

24:09.616 --> 24:13.787
[Sayid] What did he say?
— he didn't say anything.

24:14.412 --> 24:16.039
[Sayid] What is he doing?

24:16.122 --> 24:18.124
Hey! Hey!

24:21.795 --> 24:23.880
That woman just jumped over the side!

24:25.048 --> 24:28.134
Don't just stand there!
What's the matter with you people?

24:28.259 --> 24:31.596
What's wrong with you?
— why aren't you doing anything?

24:31.680 --> 24:33.223
Bring a rope! — get the rope!

24:33.306 --> 24:34.933
Get a rope! — stop!

24:35.016 --> 24:38.812
She justjumped!
— It's over. She's gone.

24:39.938 --> 24:42.190
Everybody get back to your posts.

24:45.193 --> 24:46.945
That was an order.

24:55.078 --> 24:57.706
I'm captain gault.

24:57.789 --> 25:00.333
I suppose you two have a few questions.

25:07.716 --> 25:10.844
So, what can I do for you?
— what?

25:10.927 --> 25:13.763
You wanted to speak with me.
— start with why a woman

25:13.847 --> 25:16.307
jumped over the side
and you did nothing.

25:16.433 --> 25:19.644
I didn'tjump in
or order my crew to jump in

25:19.728 --> 25:23.231
because I didn't want
to lose any more people.

25:23.314 --> 25:25.775
What exactly is going on here?

25:28.695 --> 25:32.031
Some of my crew
have been dealing with...

25:32.115 --> 25:36.035
What might best be described
as a heightened case of cabin fever.

25:38.580 --> 25:41.666
It's got to do with
the close proximity of the island.

25:41.750 --> 25:44.335
Why don't you turn around then?
— I've tried.

25:44.419 --> 25:48.673
But we have a saboteur on board. He's
done one hell of a job on my engines.

25:48.757 --> 25:51.301
I've got my crew working to repair them.

25:51.384 --> 25:56.097
And then you'll take our people home?
— then we move to safer waters.

25:56.181 --> 25:58.641
My orders.
— I don't suppose you will tell us

25:58.725 --> 26:02.854
who gave you those orders?
— sure, I will. Charles Widmore.

26:05.607 --> 26:08.485
This is Charles Widmore's boat?

26:10.361 --> 26:12.155
That's right. You know him.

26:28.713 --> 26:31.299
Do either of you know what this is?

26:31.382 --> 26:34.844
It's a flight data recorder.
Otherwise known as a black box.

26:35.512 --> 26:38.223
That's exactly what it is.

26:38.306 --> 26:40.600
Now, here's the funny thing.

26:40.683 --> 26:44.896
This black box comes
from oceanic flight 815.

26:48.483 --> 26:51.986
A salvage vessel recovered it
from the bottom of the ocean.

26:52.070 --> 26:56.950
It took a considerable amount of
Mr. Widmore's resources to procure it.

26:57.033 --> 26:59.536
It was found
with the wreckage of the plane,

26:59.619 --> 27:02.288
along with all 324 dead passengers.

27:06.251 --> 27:09.337
Not the complete story,
as you are aware, Mr. Jarrah,

27:09.420 --> 27:12.549
given the fact
that you are standing here. Breathing.

27:15.176 --> 27:17.762
The wreckage was obviously staged.

27:17.929 --> 27:21.015
Now, can you imagine
what kind of resources and manpower

27:21.099 --> 27:23.935
go into pulling off a feat
of that magnitude?

27:24.018 --> 27:26.396
Faking the recovery of a plane crash?

27:28.523 --> 27:33.111
Putting 324 families through
a grieving process based on a lie?

27:34.571 --> 27:36.656
But what's even more disturbing...

27:36.739 --> 27:42.245
Where exactly does one
come across 324 dead bodies?

27:44.163 --> 27:46.708
And that, Mr. Jarrah, Mr. Hume,

27:46.791 --> 27:50.962
is just one of the many reasons
we want Benjamin Linus.

28:03.266 --> 28:05.101
[Juliet] I'm sorry.

28:07.228 --> 28:10.273
I had to stop you any way I could.

28:13.318 --> 28:15.278
It wasn't your place to stop us.

28:16.112 --> 28:20.533
I know you don't trust me, but you need
to get off this island. We all do.

28:21.659 --> 28:25.371
You want to leave?
— more than anything.

28:27.415 --> 28:31.002
I don't know if that boat out there
is the answer, but it's something.

28:33.504 --> 28:36.549
I need to go home, and so do you.

28:37.592 --> 28:38.760
Sun...

28:40.887 --> 28:45.266
In about three weeks, you'll be
in an almost constant state of nausea.

28:45.350 --> 28:50.021
A week after, you'll experience
shortness of breath that won't go away.

28:50.146 --> 28:54.859
A week after that, you'll lose
consciousness and slip into a coma.

28:55.693 --> 28:57.695
And then, sun, you will die.

28:59.989 --> 29:03.534
And when your heart stops beating,

29:03.660 --> 29:05.411
so will the baby's.

29:08.039 --> 29:13.586
And that, sun, is why it's my business.
Because you're my patient.

29:17.215 --> 29:19.008
If you go...

29:20.760 --> 29:22.553
You will die.

29:24.889 --> 29:27.225
And your baby will never be born.

29:36.317 --> 29:38.027
[Man shouting]

30:30.496 --> 30:32.498
[Baby crying]

31:33.518 --> 31:35.937
So, what did you think of the captain?

31:36.020 --> 31:39.941
He was surprisingly forthcoming.
— yeah, he tells it like it is.

31:40.024 --> 31:43.194
Just don't piss him off,
know what I mean?

31:43.319 --> 31:47.365
I think you'll like your room.
It's on the quiet part of the ship.

31:47.490 --> 31:50.910
The ship isn't moving.
— If you say so.

32:01.212 --> 32:03.548
That shouldn't still be there. Damn it.

32:07.218 --> 32:09.011
Hey, Johnson! Is that you?

32:10.638 --> 32:13.015
Johnson! — yeah?

32:13.099 --> 32:15.101
Mop this up.

32:15.226 --> 32:19.647
Sorry. I gotta go up on deck.
— no. You're gonna mop this up.

32:43.588 --> 32:47.258
Kevin? This is... — Sayid.

32:49.594 --> 32:52.430
Desmond. — Kevin Johnson.

32:55.766 --> 32:57.393
Nice to meet you, Kevin.

33:20.208 --> 33:22.293
I made dinner.

35:35.926 --> 35:40.473
Is the baby... mine?

36:33.150 --> 36:35.820
[No audio]

38:25.763 --> 38:27.806
[Doorbell rings]

38:43.614 --> 38:44.990
[Chuckles]

38:47.201 --> 38:49.286
I can't believe you came all this way.

38:49.370 --> 38:52.248
Are you kidding?
Is anyone else coming?

38:56.835 --> 38:59.421
So where is she?

39:01.590 --> 39:04.385
[Cooing]

39:06.345 --> 39:09.390
She's awesome. — thank you.

39:12.476 --> 39:15.145
Would you like to hold her?

39:15.229 --> 39:18.148
I don't know.
I kind of have two left hands.

39:18.232 --> 39:20.025
I trust you.

39:27.157 --> 39:29.076
She looks just like Jin.

39:31.036 --> 39:33.747
Yes. She does.

39:40.129 --> 39:44.300
So I guess we should,
like, go see him.

39:46.468 --> 39:48.095
Of course.
